  causes:['Lovable: The app was built months ago on a model that now has a Deprecated badge and a retirement date, or you asked Lovable for a specific older model and the app still calls that model.','Lovable: The retirement date passed and requests were rerouted: AI activity now shows a different model, and cost or output changed.','Lovable: The retirement date passed for a "Requests fail" model (TTS, transcription, or Gemini 3.1 Flash Image) and the feature errors with the model name and its retirement date.','Lovable: You assumed the provider\'s deprecation date applies, but Lovable\'s date is earlier.','OpenAI API: A hardcoded model string in code (for example model: \'gpt-4-turbo\') from an old tutorial or AI-generated code, or the model name lives in an env var (OPENAI_MODEL) or in config on Vercel or Supabase secrets.','OpenAI API: A pinned dated snapshot of a model that is being retired, or a fine-tuned model whose base model is being retired.','OpenAI API: A preview model retired on short notice.','OpenAI API: AI coding tools (Cursor, Lovable, Bolt) often suggest older model names.'],
  steps:[{text:'Lovable: Check which models your app uses. Open More → AI in the project; the AI activity list shows the model each AI request used. After a retirement date it shows the replacement model for redirected requests, so check before the date. Or ask Lovable in the project chat which models the app\'s AI features use.'},
   {text:'Lovable: Compare those models against the table above and Lovable\'s deprecated models page.'},
   {text:'Lovable: Ask Lovable to switch. You can paste this prompt, or name the model yourself (pick from Lovable\'s "Choosing a model" docs and prefer a newer generation). Lovable updates the backend code that calls the model; a different model can change cost per request:',code:`Replace any deprecated AI models in this app with current ones.`},
   {text:'Lovable: Publish the change. Until you publish, only the preview uses the new model.'},
   {text:'Lovable: Test the AI feature in the published app and confirm in AI activity that requests now show the new model.'},
   {text:'OpenAI API: Find every model string in the repo, and also check .env files and your host\'s env vars (Vercel / Supabase Edge Function secrets):',code:`grep -rnE "gpt-(3\\.5|4|5)|\\bo[134](-mini|-pro)?\\b|gpt-image|tts-1|whisper-1|gpt-realtime|gpt-audio" --include=*.{js,ts,tsx,py} .`},
   {text:'OpenAI API: Check each model\'s shutdown date programmatically. List models and Retrieve a model return an optional shutdown_date field (YYYY-MM-DD, or null if none is announced):',code:`curl https://api.openai.com/v1/models/gpt-5-mini -H "Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_API_KEY"`},
   {text:'OpenAI API: Swap in the recommended replacement from the table. Prefer reading the model from one env var so the next swap is a one-line change. For gpt-5-pro, o3-pro and o1-pro replacements, OpenAI lists gpt-5.6-sol with reasoning.mode: pro.',code:`const model = process.env.OPENAI_MODEL || 'gpt-5.6-terra';`},
   {text:'OpenAI API: Test before the shutdown date: run the feature in a preview deploy and compare output quality, cost and latency. Replacements can respond differently.'},
   {text:'OpenAI API: For products, not models (prompts API, Agent Builder, Evals), follow OpenAI\'s migration guides linked in the sources.'}],
  related:['supabase-edge-function-non-2xx','nextjs-env-undefined-client','vercel-works-locally-fails-deploy','cursor-model-overloaded'],
